// PIN ZYVM-002 — the message named the code route, not the operator.
//
// The VM read every arithmetic operand through one macro whose String branch
// carried the guidance for `+`, so `-"a"` was refused with advice about
// concatenating strings. The tree-walker said `negation requires numeric
// operand`. Unary minus is not in the operator matrix — it crosses BINARY
// operators — so nothing held this down. Closed 2026-08-30.
x = -"a"
>> x ¶
